  "note": "Complete joint Laplace law for every finite k>=1 of independent continuing Brownian walkers on a normalized circle, arbitrary fixed distinct labeled seeds and independent-uniform or equidistant seeds. Explicit finite permutation sums and deterministic exit-kernel integrals give each coefficient, with cumulative physical clocks, a uniform factorial outer remainder and compact-simplex moment determinacy. Earlier painting and classical methods credited: Gomes Júnior–Lucena–da Silva–Hilhorst (1996); Miller (2013); Chatterjee–Nabahi–Terlov (2026); Baccara (2026); Si (2026); Fitzsimmons–Pitman (1999); Régnier–Dolgushev–Redner–Bénichou (2022). No named density, fast algorithm or certified inner quadrature. Finite-model and scalar diagnostics supplement the written proof; they do not prove the Brownian theorem. The dated bounded audit found no prior complete general target law; no absolute/exclusive priority or independent discovery is established. Gomes1996/Dicker2006 fulltext403 and Zenodo registry403 remain limitations; reopen priority on a concrete general-resolution source. Extensive AI use; unrefereed and no conventional human peer review. Original reported1/5; present import adds0 central turns.",
